hk: leave the barrier after vkCmdDispatch pending

Every compute launch ends with a CDM barrier, so dispatches with nothing
between them still run one after another. Vulkan orders them only across
a pipeline barrier or event, and those already end the control stream.
vkCmdDispatch now leaves its barrier pending: the next launch that must be
ordered (every internal one: meta operations, queries, the geometry and
tessellation stages) or the end of the stream emits it, and dispatches in
between may overlap. This is what Metal's concurrent dispatch mode does;
on an M2 Pro it costs 0.14 us a dispatch against 1.3-1.5 us serial.
Scratch is per hardware subgroup slot, so overlapping kernels don't share
it.

Applies after mesa-agx-g14x-metal-cdm-barrier.

